{
  "about": [
    "Design claims for the side-by-side check (scripts/verify/side-by-side.mjs). One entry per component of handoff section 4 'Components to build in /components/lp'.",
    "design.state is a prototype state (scripts/verify/design-render.mjs): route, plan, role, an optional seed merged into the prototype's store and optional steps. design.locator is a Playwright selector that resolves to exactly one visible element in the design DOM; part locators are relative to it.",
    "app.locator finds the element on the app's /specimens page ([data-specimen=\"<id>\"] unless stated). A marker on an unstyled wrapper is followed down to the first element that draws something. app locators may be a list: the first that resolves wins, so a data-part or data-specimen can come first and a semantic fallback (a role, a heading, the first child) after it. Part app locators are relative to the app element ([data-part=\"<name>\"] unless stated).",
    "properties are compared by computed style and gate the run. Group names expand: padding, border, border-top, border-width, border-style, border-color, border-radius, gap. box-width and box-height are the rendered box, for elements whose width is not a computed length (icons).",
    "expect overrides the design's value where a higher source corrects it (handoff section 4 component spec, a contrast fix, or an owner's answer in REUSE_EVALUATION 2.0); the app is held to expect, the design value is reported beside it.",
    "excluded lists what is deliberately not compared, each with its reason. Widths of layout containers are never compared: handoff section 11, Whole product, 'A fixed 1280 px layout -> Responsive from 360 px'.",
    "tolerance is the share of differing pixels the visual sheet calls close enough. It is informational and never fails the run; copy, data and icons differ between the design and the app by design.",
    "mask lists design regions painted over before the pixel diff because handoff section 11 removes them."
  ],
  "viewport": {
    "width": 1280,
    "height": 900
  },
  "claims": [
    {
      "id": "topbar",
      "what": "TopBar: the sticky strip across the top (page colour at 92 % with a 10 px blur), holding the --bar pill. data-specimen on the sticky strip; data-part=\"bar\" on the pill.",
      "design": {
        "state": {
          "route": "home",
          "plan": "team"
        },
        "locator": "span[title=\"Plan and billing\"] >> xpath=../.."
      },
      "app": {
        "locator": "[data-specimen=\"topbar\"]"
      },
      "properties": [
        "background-color",
        "backdrop-filter",
        "padding-top",
        "padding-left",
        "padding-right"
      ],
      "excluded": {
        "position, top": "the specimens page draws the bar in place so it does not cover the specimens; sticky is the shell's behaviour (handoff section 4 TopBar), checked in the app, not here",
        "padding-bottom": "the design's strip pads 14 px all round; where the space under the bar lives is the shell's rhythm",
        "width": "handoff section 11 Whole product: fixed 1280 px layout -> responsive; widths are checked by mobile.mjs and a person",
        "z-index": "stacking is the shell's concern, not the bar's look"
      },
      "parts": [
        {
          "name": "bar",
          "design": "xpath=./div[1]",
          "app": [
            "[data-part=\"bar\"]",
            "xpath=./*[1]"
          ],
          "properties": [
            "font-family",
            "background-color",
            "border",
            "border-radius",
            "padding",
            "min-height",
            "column-gap"
          ],
          "excluded": {
            "max-width": "handoff section 11 Whole product (responsive): the 1240 px cap is the page's content width, held by the shell",
            "the layout and width toggles": "handoff section 11 Whole product: 'A sidebar layout, a width switch and an Appearance tab -> The top bar only'",
            "the 360 navigation item": "handoff section 11 Whole product: 'A 360 item in the navigation -> Nothing'"
          }
        }
      ],
      "mask": [
        "div[title=\"Switch to a vertical menu\"]",
        "div[title=\"Extend to full width\"]",
        "span[title=\"Plan and billing\"] >> xpath=../div[2]/div[normalize-space()=\"360\"]"
